WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.820
- I have no agenda here
to tell you this, but,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.310
I had never met you until
just a few moments ago.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.510
- Yeah.
- But,

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:10.250
you come across, on television,
as exactly as you are,

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.290
as full of joy

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.700
and you will have a career
as long as you want one

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.022
in this business.
(audience cheering)

00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:19.440
'Cause people see you on television,

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.280
they see you on television,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.150
you can't, you can't
look at your personality

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.290
and not be joyful.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.600
It's happening, you don't
get depressed looking at you,

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.690
with me, people go to the other room.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.730
- No, with you they start chanting

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.938
until you can't be. (laughing)

00:00:34.938 --> 00:00:36.804
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:00:36.804 --> 00:00:38.551
- That's my favorite part.

00:00:38.551 --> 00:00:39.384
- Yeah. (chuckling)

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:40.780
- Wait, you also made a movie?

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.560
- And so did you, fancy pants.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.100
- Mm-hmm, and mine is
contractual obligated,

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.880
it was horrible.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.874
How was yours?
- Horrible.

00:00:49.874 --> 00:00:51.324
- Yeah.
- Yes.

00:00:51.324 --> 00:00:52.323
- Radsies for the both of us.
- Yeah.

00:00:53.539 --> 00:00:55.897
- What was your movie about?

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:56.730
- What was my movie about?
- Yeah.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.700
- It was about two hours.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.880
It was about two hours
too long, is what it was.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.330
No, it was called "Ringmaster"

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.010
and it came out right when my show was

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.420
really doing well.
- Oh.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.127
- And so they wanted me
to make a movie about it,

00:01:09.127 --> 00:01:12.700
"Ringmaster", because it's
a circus, my show, so,

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.220
and that's what we did.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.710
I never made a movie before, so,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.210
when I started doing the movie,

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.800
then I would joke around,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.190
I'd say, "Now, when are the Oscars?"

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:26.350
So I got a buddy of mine to
write an acceptance speech

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:27.850
for me.
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.160
- 'Cause I was confident.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.530
But he wrote the speech and
the first thing in the speech

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.430
is, "I'd like to thank
my wife, Connie Chung."

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:39.420
(audience groaning)
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.832
I love Maury, but I'm not Maury.

00:01:41.832 --> 00:01:42.665
(audience laughing)

